-- Purpose: Seed the CONFIG half of the JWT_SCAFFOLD_CONFIG row, then register the ORDS JWT
--   profile from it. Deliberately writes NO key material - see below.
-- Approach: MERGE on config_id = 1 so the script is idempotent and re-runnable, followed by
--   delete_jwt_profile + create_jwt_profile reading the row just written.
-- Reason: This script is committed, so it must never carry a private key. Key columns are
--   populated separately by bin/ensure-auth-key.sh and are left untouched here, so a redeploy
--   never rotates a live key. create_jwt_profile SNAPSHOTS this row - it is not a
--   view over it - so seeding config without re-registering leaves validation on stale values.
--   The two must move together; see planning/spec-patch-04-auth-config-derivation.md section 5.3.
-- Expected objects:
--   JWT_SCAFFOLD_CONFIG (one row, config_id = 1)
--   ORDS JWT profile (schema-level, one per schema)
-- Risk: Medium. Re-registering the JWT profile invalidates nothing already issued, but a wrong
--   jwk_url produces tokens that fail validation with a generic ORDS 401 and no useful diagnostic.
-- Prior history checked: Search db-history for prior 80_standalone runs in this environment.
